{
  "id": "m9l1",
  "title": {
    "es": "Importar módulos: math y random",
    "en": "Importing modules: math and random"
  },
  "theory": {
    "es": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Reutilizar código: import"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Python trae una enorme **librería estándar**. Con `import modulo` accedes a sus funciones como `modulo.funcion(...)`. También puedes `from modulo import funcion`."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "import math",
          "print(math.sqrt(16))",
          "print(math.pi)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "4.0",
          "3.141592653589793"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Números: math"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`math` ofrece `sqrt`, `ceil`, `floor`, `factorial`, `pi`… y `math.hypot(a, b)` calcula la hipotenusa."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "import math",
          "print(math.ceil(4.1), math.floor(4.9))",
          "print(math.hypot(3, 4))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "5 4",
          "5.0"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Azar: random"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`random` genera valores aleatorios: `random.randint(a, b)`, `random.choice(lista)`, `random.shuffle(lista)`. Con `random.seed(x)` los resultados son **reproducibles**."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "import random",
          "random.seed(0)",
          "valor = random.randint(1, 6)  # entre 1 y 6"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Usa `random.seed(...)` cuando necesites resultados repetibles (por ejemplo, en pruebas)."
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Reuse code: import"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Python ships a huge **standard library**. With `import module` you access its functions as `module.function(...)`. You can also `from module import function`."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "import math",
          "print(math.sqrt(16))",
          "print(math.pi)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "4.0",
          "3.141592653589793"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Numbers: math"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`math` offers `sqrt`, `ceil`, `floor`, `factorial`, `pi`… and `math.hypot(a, b)` computes the hypotenuse."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "import math",
          "print(math.ceil(4.1), math.floor(4.9))",
          "print(math.hypot(3, 4))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "5 4",
          "5.0"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Randomness: random"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`random` generates random values: `random.randint(a, b)`, `random.choice(list)`, `random.shuffle(list)`. With `random.seed(x)` results are **reproducible**."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "import random",
          "random.seed(0)",
          "valor = random.randint(1, 6)  # between 1 and 6"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Use `random.seed(...)` when you need repeatable results (for example, in tests)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "m9l1e1",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `hipotenusa(a, b)` que devuelva la hipotenusa usando `math` (importa `math`).",
        "en": "Define `hipotenusa(a, b)` returning the hypotenuse using `math` (import `math`)."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "import math",
        "",
        "def hipotenusa(a, b):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "import math",
        "",
        "def hipotenusa(a, b):",
        "    return math.hypot(a, b)"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "math.hypot(a, b) lo calcula directamente."
        ],
        "en": [
          "math.hypot(a, b) computes it directly."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "function": "hipotenusa",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                3,
                4
              ],
              "expected": 5.0
            },
            {
              "args": [
                6,
                8
              ],
              "expected": 10.0
            },
            {
              "args": [
                5,
                12
              ],
              "expected": 13.0
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m9l1e2",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `redondea_arriba(x)` que devuelva `x` redondeado hacia arriba al entero más cercano (usa `math.ceil`).",
        "en": "Define `redondea_arriba(x)` returning `x` rounded up to the nearest integer (use `math.ceil`)."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "import math",
        "",
        "def redondea_arriba(x):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "import math",
        "",
        "def redondea_arriba(x):",
        "    return math.ceil(x)"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "math.ceil(4.1) == 5.",
          "math.ceil(4.0) == 4."
        ],
        "en": [
          "math.ceil(4.1) == 5.",
          "math.ceil(4.0) == 4."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "function": "redondea_arriba",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                4.1
              ],
              "expected": 5
            },
            {
              "args": [
                4.0
              ],
              "expected": 4
            },
            {
              "args": [
                -1.5
              ],
              "expected": -1
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}